# 🧪 Development Approach

GIANTBOUND is planned to go through several testing stages:

🧪 Prototype → 🧩 Beta → 🔬 Alpha → 🎮 Demo → 🌎 Public Game

🧪 Prototype

The Prototype stage is mainly for testing individual functions and systems.

The goal is to make sure important features actually work before trying to build the full game.

# 🧩 Beta

More systems are combined and tested together.

# 🔬 Alpha

The game becomes more advanced and receives deeper testing and improvements.

# 🎮 Demo

A playable version will be tested with family members and other selected testers.

# 🌎 Public Game

After enough testing, fixing, balancing, and improvement, the game can move toward a public release.

---

# 🗿 Giant Gameplay

The Giant is designed to have active gameplay rather than simply waiting for the Tiny Players.

The Giant can influence the environment through abilities, obstacles, hazards, and other systems.

The goal is to make Giant gameplay powerful but still allow Tiny Players to use skill, teamwork, movement, and strategy to counter it.

---

# 👤 Tiny Player Gameplay

Tiny Players use their smaller size as an advantage.

Possible gameplay includes:

- 🏃 Parkour
- 🧗 Climbing and traversal
- ⚔️ Counterplay
- 🎒 Gadgets and abilities
- 🛡️ Defensive items
- 🤝 Teamwork
- 🎯 Objectives
- 🎁 Temporary upgrades and lucky items

Tiny Players should have meaningful ways to react to Giant actions instead of simply waiting for the match to end.

---

# 🗺️ Map System

Maps are designed around the Giant/Tiny scale difference.

Possible environments include:

- 🏘️ Settlements
- 🌲 Forests
- 🏚️ Abandoned structures
- 🌉 Bridges
- 🪨 Rocky areas
- 🏢 Buildings
- 🌎 Large environmental areas

Maps should provide multiple routes whenever possible so that blocking one path does not automatically make the entire map impossible.

The scale difference should affect gameplay:

- Ordinary objects can become huge obstacles for Tiny Players.
- Giant movement can change available routes.
- Structures can provide climbing and hiding opportunities.
- Environmental objects can interact with abilities and powers.

---

# 🏆 Rewards & Progression

GIANTBOUND is planned to have long-term progression.

Possible systems include:

- 🪙 Coins
- ⭐ XP
- 📈 Levels
- 🏅 Achievements
- 🎁 Match rewards
- 🎨 Cosmetic rewards
- 🗿 Giant customization
- 👤 Tiny Player customization
- ✨ Effects
- 😎 Emotes
- 🧢 Accessories
- 🎉 Event cosmetics

Optional Robux purchases may be used for cosmetics and customization.

The goal is to avoid making the core gameplay pay-to-win.

Basic progression:

🎮 Matches → ⭐ XP → 📈 Level Up → 🎁 Rewards / Unlocks

